{#
  T-7.02 — «الأسئلة الشائعة», the FAQ accordion.

  | Variable                    | Type    | Description                        |
  |-----------------------------|---------|------------------------------------|
  | component.title             | ?string | Section heading                    |
  | component.intro             | ?string | The paragraph under it             |
  | component.items[].question  | string  | The question, as drawn             |
  | component.items[].answer    | string  | The answer. Line breaks become a list |
  | position                    | int     | Sorting number, from zero          |

  IT IS A REGISTERED SECTION AND NOT `pages/faq.twig`, FOR THE REASON T-7.06
  ALREADY RECORDED AND THE OWNER CONFIRMED. **Salla's page set is fixed and a
  theme cannot mint a `/faq` route** — the backlog names a page file that could
  never be rendered, the same mistake it made for the stories feed and the
  tracking page. Registered as a component, the merchant places it on the CMS page
  they created for it, which is the arrangement T-7.01 built the shell for and
  OP-3 settled. **The backlog's own «New sections: FAQ (registered)» line already
  says so**; only its «Files affected» disagreed.

  IT IS BUTTONS AND NOT `<details>`, WHICH REVERSES THIS THEME'S USUAL
  PREFERENCE AND THE CRITERION IS WHY. T-2.10 and T-4.17 both took the element
  that already has the behaviour. Here the criterion asks for `aria-expanded`
  **and `aria-controls`**, and `<summary>` supplies the first and cannot supply
  the second — a `<details>` panel has no id relationship to state. The other two
  criteria push the same way: a height transition needs a panel it can size, and
  deep-linking needs to open an entry that the UA has not already decided about.
  So the disclosure is built, and `accordion.js` is the whole of what `<details>`
  would have given free.

  THE ANSWER'S LINE BREAKS BECOME A LIST, WHICH IS THE ARTBOARD'S OWN READING.
  «كم مدة الشحن؟» is drawn as two bulleted lines; every other answer is one
  paragraph. A merchant writing two lines in one field means two points, and a
  `<ul>` says that to a screen reader where a `<br>` says nothing at all.
#}
{% set faq_items = component.items|default([]) %}

{% if faq_items|length %}
    <section data-testid="store-home-faq"
             class="s-block faq container"
             {% if component.title %}aria-labelledby="faq-{{ position }}-title"{% endif %}>
        <div class="account-panel faq__panel">
            {% if component.title %}
                <h2 class="faq__title" id="faq-{{ position }}-title">{{ component.title }}</h2>
            {% endif %}

            {% if component.intro %}
                <p class="faq__intro">{{ component.intro }}</p>
            {% endif %}

            <div class="faq__list">
                {% for item in faq_items %}
                    {% set faq_id = 'faq-' ~ position ~ '-' ~ loop.index %}

                    <div class="faq__item">
                        <h3 class="faq__question">
                            {#
                              The heading wraps the button rather than the button
                              wrapping the heading: a screen reader's heading list
                              should carry the questions, and a control inside a
                              heading is still a control.
                            #}
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="faq__trigger"
                                    id="{{ faq_id }}-trigger"
                                    aria-expanded="false"
                                    aria-controls="{{ faq_id }}"
                                    data-faq-trigger>
                                <span class="faq__number" aria-hidden="true">{{ loop.index }}/</span>
                                <span class="faq__text">{{ item.question }}</span>
                                <span class="disclosure-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            </button>
                        </h3>

                        {#
                          `hidden` and not a class: a collapsed answer must leave
                          the accessibility tree, or it is only visually collapsed
                          and a screen reader reads every answer on the page at
                          once. The script removes it and animates the wrapper.
                        #}
                        <div class="faq__answer"
                             id="{{ faq_id }}"
                             role="region"
                             aria-labelledby="{{ faq_id }}-trigger"
                             hidden>
                            <div class="faq__answer-inner">
                                {% set faq_lines = item.answer|split('\n') %}

                                {% if faq_lines|length > 1 %}
                                    <ul>
                                        {% for line in faq_lines %}
                                            {% if line|trim %}
                                                <li>{{ line|trim }}</li>
                                            {% endif %}
                                        {% endfor %}
                                    </ul>
                                {% else %}
                                    <p>{{ item.answer }}</p>
                                {% endif %}
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>

        {#
          FAQPage schema. Emitted from the same fields the accordion renders, so
          the structured data and the page cannot disagree — the failure mode
          that gets a store's rich results withdrawn. `json_encode` escapes the
          merchant's text, which is why this is safe to emit raw.
        #}
        <script type="application/ld+json">
            {{ {
                '@context': 'https://schema.org',
                '@type': 'FAQPage',
                'mainEntity': faq_items|map(item => {
                    '@type': 'Question',
                    'name': item.question,
                    'acceptedAnswer': { '@type': 'Answer', 'text': item.answer }
                })|filter(entry => entry.name is not empty)|values
            }|json_encode|raw }}
        </script>
    </section>
{% endif %}
